{{!-- A closing {{/action}} line is removed with its line break, so two blank lines follow each, to end the paragraph of the button. --}}
Each button below runs logic programs on this card and its child cards. A button that works shows a message and refreshes the card; a button that fails shows an error message and changes nothing, unless it says otherwise.

== Workflow

Approve moves this card from Draft to Approved; its workflow state changes at the top of the card.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Approve",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    transition({{{cardKey}}}, "Approve").
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


== Creating cards

Add page creates a child card Untitled page under this card, and the message links to it.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Add page",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    create({{{cardKey}}}, "test/templates/page").
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


Add named page creates a child card in its first program, and its second program names it Named page and gives it the label named.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Add named page",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    create({{{cardKey}}}, "test/templates/page").
    {{/quoted}},
    {{#quoted}}
    setField(K, "title", "Named page") :- created(K, _, "test/templates/page", _, _).
    addLabel(K, "named") :- created(K, _, "test/templates/page", _, _).
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


== Fields

Set fields sets Short text of this card to Set by an action and Integer to 42; the 42 is given as text and converted to a number.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Set fields",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    setField({{{cardKey}}}, "test/fieldTypes/shortText", "Set by an action").
    setField({{{cardKey}}}, "test/fieldTypes/integer", "42").
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


== Labels

Add label gives this card the label reviewed.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Add label",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    addLabel({{{cardKey}}}, "reviewed").
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


Remove label takes the label reviewed away again and keeps the label demo.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Remove label",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    removeLabel({{{cardKey}}}, "reviewed").
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


== Links

Add link links this card to its child card Link target; the link shows under Outbound.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Add link",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    addLink({{{cardKey}}}, T, "test/linkTypes/test") :- parent(T, {{{cardKey}}}), field(T, "title", "Link target").
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


Remove link removes that link again.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Remove link",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    removeLink({{{cardKey}}}, T, "test/linkTypes/test") :- parent(T, {{{cardKey}}}), field(T, "title", "Link target").
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


== Content

Set content replaces the content of the child card Notes with a short checklist.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Set content",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    setContent(N, {{#quoted}}
== Checklist

. Read the demo.
. Click every button.
{{/quoted}}) :- parent(N, {{{cardKey}}}), field(N, "title", "Notes").
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


Copy content replaces the content of Notes with the content of the child card Source text.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Copy content",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    copyContent(N, S) :- parent(N, {{{cardKey}}}), field(N, "title", "Notes"), parent(S, {{{cardKey}}}), field(S, "title", "Source text").
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


== Ranking and moving

Rank first puts the child card Movable page first among the children of this card.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Rank first",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    rankFirst(M) :- parent(M, {{{cardKey}}}), field(M, "title", "Movable page").
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


Move moves Movable page under the child card Link target in the card tree.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Move",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    move(M, T) :- parent(M, {{{cardKey}}}), field(M, "title", "Movable page"), parent(T, {{{cardKey}}}), field(T, "title", "Link target").
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


== Nothing to change

Add label demo adds a label that this card already has, so nothing changes and the message says that the action ran.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Add label demo",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    addLabel({{{cardKey}}}, "demo").
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


== Failures

Approve again works only while this card is Draft; after Approve above, it fails with a message that the workflow has no Approve transition from state Approved.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Approve again",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    transition({{{cardKey}}}, "Approve").
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


Set a missing field sets Failure message, which is not a field of this card's type, and fails with a message that it is neither title nor a custom field of card type All data types.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Set a missing field",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    setField({{{cardKey}}}, "test/fieldTypes/failureMessage", "Oops").
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


Set text into Integer sets Integer to the text many and fails with a message that many is not a valid integer value.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Set text into Integer",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    setField({{{cardKey}}}, "test/fieldTypes/integer", "many").
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


Set two values sets Short text to both One and Two in one program and fails with a message that the field is set to two different values.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Set two values",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    setField({{{cardKey}}}, "test/fieldTypes/shortText", "One").
    setField({{{cardKey}}}, "test/fieldTypes/shortText", "Two").
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


Edit locked field changes Field to edit of the child card Locked card, which a deny rule forbids, and fails with the rule's message: The field Field to edit of this card is locked.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Edit locked field",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    setField(L, "test/fieldTypes/shortText", "Changed") :- parent(L, {{{cardKey}}}), field(L, "title", "Locked card").
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


Run a broken program runs a program with a syntax error and fails with a message that starts with Parsing failed.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Run a broken program",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    transition({{{cardKey}}}, "Approve"
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


Label the template card adds a label to the card of the Action macro demo template, which cannot be changed, and fails with a message that the card is a template card, or a module card when module-test is installed as a module.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Label the template card",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    addLabel(T, "reviewed") :- parent(T, "test/templates/actionDemo").
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}


Fail in program 2 adds the label partial to this card in its first program, then fails in its second program on the text many in Integer, with a message that ends: Without autocommit, the changes of the earlier programs were kept. Without autocommit, the label partial stays; with autocommit, nothing changes.

{{#action}}
  "buttonLabel": "Fail in program 2",
  "actions": [
    {{#quoted}}
    addLabel({{{cardKey}}}, "partial").
    {{/quoted}},
    {{#quoted}}
    setField({{{cardKey}}}, "test/fieldTypes/integer", "many").
    {{/quoted}}
  ]
{{/action}}
